  { q: 'What is the fee for a death certificate through eSathi and CSC?', a: 'Applying yourself on eSathi costs about ₹10 to ₹15. If a CSC or Jan Seva Kendra operator applies for you, the government fee is ₹30 and the centre may add a facilitation charge of roughly ₹30 to ₹50. Anything far above this is overcharging — you can complain on the CM Helpline 1076.' },
  { q: 'Can I download the death certificate online after approval?', a: 'Yes. Once the status shows the certificate has been generated, log in to your eSathi account, open the completed application and use the Print option to save the digitally signed PDF. Certificates issued through the portal also become available in DigiLocker after a few days.' },
  { q: 'There is a spelling mistake in the name on the death certificate. Can it be corrected?', a: 'Yes, minor errors such as spelling of the name, a wrong date entry or an incomplete address can be corrected by applying for correction with supporting documents, such as the hospital record and the Aadhaar of the deceased. Always check the downloaded certificate immediately, because corrections are simplest soon after issue.' },
